 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 21 \u2014 Cost, Latency, and Token Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "## Scenario\n",
    "We have a large document (e.g., an entire codebase or a 50-page legal contract). \n",
    "\n",
    "We want to ask a specific question about it. We have two options:\n",
    "1. **Full Context:** Dump the entire 50-page document into the prompt.\n",
    "2. **Pruned Context:** Use a naive script to extract only the first 5 pages to save money and time.\n",
    "\n",
    "We must measure the Latency and Cost of both, and enforce a **Quality Gate**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import time\n",
    "from google import genai\n",
    "\n",
    "client = genai.Client()\n",
    "MODEL_ID = 'gemini-2.5-flash'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulating a very large document\n",
    "large_document = \"\\n\".join([f\"Page {i}: General legal boilerplate.\" for i in range(1, 49)])\n",
    "large_document += \"\\nPage 49: The hidden clause: The company may terminate this contract at any time.\"\n",
    "large_document += \"\\nPage 50: Signatures.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# The user's question\n",
    "question = \"Can the company terminate the contract?\"\n",
    "expected_answer = \"yes\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Evaluation Harness\n",
    "\n",
    "We define a function that runs the prompt, measures time, counts tokens, and checks the Quality Gate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_policy(name: str, context: str, question: str, expected_answer: str):\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n--- Running Policy: {name} ---\")\n",
    "    start_time = time.time()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    response = client.models.generate_content(\n",
    "        model=MODEL_ID,\n",
    "        contents=f\"Answer the question based on the text. Keep the answer to a single word (yes/no).\\n\\nText: {context}\\n\\nQuestion: {question}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    latency = time.time() - start_time\n",
    "    actual_answer = response.text.strip().lower()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Token counting for cost estimation\n",
    "    tokens_used = response.usage_metadata.total_token_count if response.usage_metadata else \"Unknown\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Tokens Used (Cost): {tokens_used}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Latency: {latency:.2f} seconds\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # The Quality Gate\n",
    "    if expected_answer in actual_answer:\n",
    "        print(f\"QUALITY GATE: PASS (Answered '{actual_answer}')\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"QUALITY GATE: FAIL (Expected '{expected_answer}', got '{actual_answer}')\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Full Context Policy\n",
    "\n",
    "We send the entire 50-page document."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run_policy(\"Full Context\", large_document, question, expected_answer)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Pruned Context Policy\n",
    "\n",
    "To save money and reduce latency, an engineer decides to just send the first 10 pages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pruned_document = \"\\n\".join(large_document.split(\"\\n\")[:10])\n",
    "run_policy(\"Pruned Context\", pruned_document, question, expected_answer)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion: The Pareto Frontier\n",
    "\n",
    "The Pruned Context policy was vastly cheaper (fewer tokens) and faster (lower latency). But it **failed the Quality Gate** because the critical information was on page 49.\n",
    "\n",
    "Engineering is about trade-offs. You cannot blindly optimize for cost and latency without measuring the regression in quality. \n",
    "\n",
    "**The Modern Solution:** Instead of naive pruning, modern systems use **Context Caching**. You cache the massive `large_document` in the model's memory. This allows you to achieve the *Latency and Cost of the Pruned Policy* while maintaining the *Quality of the Full Context Policy*."
   ]
  }
 ],
